{"title":"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Eight <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/8/8a8df7312744a199daa5c8008af5b9b4798bfd64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> square tiles are arranged as shown so their outside edges form a polygon with a perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> units.  Two additional tiles of the same size are added to the figure so that at least one side of each tile is shared with a side of one of the squares in the original figure.  Which of the following could be the perimeter of the new figure?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08aaee15864e18a32aa70fb9c2f14e3dcc4a29c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] for (int a=1; a &lt;= 4; ++a) {     draw((a,0)--(a,2)); } draw((0,0)--(4,0)); draw((0,1)--(5,1)); draw((1,2)--(5,2)); draw((0,0)--(0,1)); draw((5,1)--(5,2)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"102\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f205b3e32d513d2bffa1fd2b350c3c4cf3f2fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 15 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 17 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 18 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 19 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One such figure would be\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d7bc4df2b6e03187fbb098512c4bbc4a4571366.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] for (int a=1; a &lt;= 4; ++a) {     draw((a,0)--(a,3)); } draw((0,0)--(4,0)); draw((0,1)--(5,1)); draw((1,2)--(5,2)); draw((0,0)--(0,1)); draw((5,1)--(5,2)); draw((2,3)--(1,3)); draw((4,3)--(3,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p>The perimeter of this figure is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d33e70c5266e1978b0ea5d4e682f8dcf6754b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C)}\\ 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we attach a square to one side, one side will be covered, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more sides will be added, resulting in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe54585e0c171194b0e07cc59767d097999658cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> perimeter. If we attach a square to two sides, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides are covered and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides are attached, so the perimeter don't change. There is no possibility of attaching a square to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides, so we can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/354b238fd965791b8aac2e7b2c877e98564afc6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14,16,18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" /> as the perimeter so the only answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d33e70c5266e1978b0ea5d4e682f8dcf6754b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C)}\\ 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~TheRealMee\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME\" title=\"1992 AJHSME\">1992 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=